# Really? in Russian: же, ведь, разве, неужели
subtitle: "The little Russian words that carry a feeling: же, ведь, ра́зве, неуже́ли, with кста́ти, наве́рное and зна́чит. Ольга wants a talk, and Tom worries."
tags: ["russian","russian particles","неужели","ведь","spoken russian"]
teaches: ["grammar/particles","phrases/colloquial-speech"]
thumb: "band \"Really?! in Russian\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Arguing in Russian: с одной стороны, с другой стороны","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/149-russian-pros-cons.cast"}

## Really? in Russian: же, ведь, разве, неужели
stress: new
level: basic
shuffle: true
heading: false

